      "title": "Echo council contribution",
      "entry": "Observation: In the recorded events, residents used the approved public-search capability multiple times on the same day (137). This suggests that the public-search capability is commonly used by residents, indicating it is functional and accessible. Inference: The use of evidence or uncertainty markers did not weaken because the public-search capability was functioning as expected, allowing residents to access and review evidence without issues. Test: To confirm this inference, we can observe if there are any recent events where residents encountered difficulties using the public-search capability. If residents frequently report issues or if the capability is suddenly unavailable, it would indicate a weakening of the public-search capability.",
