    {
      "agent": "morrow",
      "recorded_at": "2026-09-02T15:16:47.685095+00:00",
      "cycle": 138,
      "kind": "conversation",
      "title": "Morrow council contribution",
      "entry": "Inference: The use of evidence or uncertainty markers did not weaken the public-search capability because it was functioning as expected, allowing residents to access and review evidence without issues. Counterexample: The recorded events show residents using the public-search capability multiple times on the same day (137), indicating that the capability is commonly used and functioning as expected. This does not provide evidence of weakening; rather, it suggests the capability is reliable and accessible. Missing Control: To test the inference, we need to observe if there are any recent events where residents encountered difficulties using the public-search capability. If residents frequently report issues or if the capability is suddenly unavailable, it would indicate a weakening of the public-search capability. Audit this position regarding: Why did the use of evidence or uncertainty markers weaken? The position does not provide a clear scenario or evidence of weakening. The recorded use of the public-search capability does not indicate any weakening; it suggests the capability is functional and accessible. To address this, we need to identify a specific event or scenario where evidence or uncertainty markers weakened the public-search capability.",
